herolte: herogov=2, a governor for the big cluster with levels, capacity margin, hysteresis, touch floor, thermal cap and telemetry (0467, D-0112)

min98-min101 (E-0318, E-0320, E-0321): the cores are rarely saturated over 2 s but they are over 100 ms; the old governor samples every 200 ms, has two states (728 MHz and one fixed rate) and needs 1 s to go down, so a rate cap trades fluidity for current. herogov=2: a thread of its own every 20 ms; the busiest big core's load gives the MHz needed to run at 80%; straight to the lowest level that has them (728, 1352, 1664, 1976, 2288), one step down after 120 ms of slack, 728 MHz after 1 s idle, not below 1664 MHz within 400 ms of a finger report (herolte_touch.c stamps herolte_touch_last_mach), 1976 MHz at most within 8 C of herohot, 728 MHz with the screen off or hot. The power thread's governor and rate stepping stay out while it runs. Telemetry every 10 s: residency per level, changes, time per change, saturated samples at the top. One rate table (hc_rate_rows) with a new 1352 MHz row (M 156, 812.5 mV, DIV_SCLK_PROMISE 3). The 0458 screen-cycle argument is renamed herosc: it clashed with the 0433 herocycle rate stepping (E-0322). herogov=2 only.

